---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const asset='/equipment/09-04/',ds='https://download.tek.com/datasheet/MSO6B-Datasheet-EN-US-48W-61716-10.pdf';
const refs=[
 ['front','01 / Bench configuration','Original front three-quarter reconstruction. The maker’s cover photo shows the eight-channel sibling, not this four-channel configuration; side vents, grip and shell proportions follow the shared housing. Four FlexChannels follow the MSO64B specification, p. 37. Connector spacing is estimated.',ds+'#page=1'],
 ['controls','02 / Operator controls','Original control-panel rendering. Compare the grouped trigger, vertical, timebase, single and run controls with the family panel photograph on p. 9. Only CH1 is acquired in this bench; the other connectors are inspection geometry.',ds+'#page=9'],
 ['rear','03 / Rear I/O','Original rear view. The photograph on p. 34 and port table on p. 60 establish the IEC, LAN, USB, video and reference/aux connections. AFG is not enabled; its optional jack is depicted blank. Vents and port coordinates are inferred.',ds+'#page=34'],
 ['ports','04 / Probe connection','Original working-area view. One TPP1000 passive probe is fitted to CH1. The cable routing and shape are illustrative; the compensator signal post is on the lower front right. No image licensing is implied.',ds+'#page=60']
];
const specs=[
 ['Assembled envelope','454 W × 371 H × 205 D mm','Geometry; handle up, feet folded, excluding removable probe. Width is between handle hubs; depth to front of knobs.','61'],
 ['Active LCD','15.6 in (395 mm nominal), 1920 × 1080','Geometry; 16:9 active panel. Bezel, control diameters, vent and connector spacing inferred from family photographs.','55'],
 ['Analog inputs / bandwidth','4 FlexChannels / 1 GHz','Configuration: 6-BW-1000 option. CH1 fitted; no digital pod or licensed AFG modeled.','63'],
 ['Nominal digitizer','12-bit ADC','Behavior: a uniform 4096-code software quantizer, not a clone of vendor High Res filtering. Real vertical resolution depends on acquisition mode/rate.','37'],
 ['Probe-compensation output','0–2.5 V, 1 kHz, 1 kΩ typical','Behavior: nominal unloaded levels and source impedance. 50% duty is a fixture assumption, not a tolerance.','60'],
 ['Physical probe','TPP1000, 10× passive, 1 GHz','Loading: nominal 10 MΩ at the tip for compensation check. Tip capacitance is <4 pF and the stock cable is 1.3 m; both are omitted from this low-frequency model.','63']
];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Digital oscilloscope laboratory" subtitle="" description="Operate a reference-informed MSO64B measurement bench and export a triggered voltage capture." wide={true}>
<article id="scope09" class="equipment">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/">← Equipment 09-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#evidence">Reference sheet</a><a href="#verification">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">09-04 / ELECTRICAL INSTRUMENTATION</span><h2>One pulse, two cursors</h2><p class="eq-lede">Acquire a trace on the Tektronix MSO64B. The four-input, 1 GHz instrument has a TPP1000 on CH1 and a 1 kHz example ready to measure. Try reversing the trigger edge, then inspect the same pulse at a different timebase.</p></header>
<div class="scope-grid">
<section class="s-panel"><p class="eq-meta">01 / INSTRUMENT</p><h3>6 Series B MSO</h3><div class="scope-view"><canvas id="scope-3d" aria-label="Orbitable MSO64B instrument"></canvas></div>
<div class="tools">{[['reset','Reset view'],['front','Front'],['controls','Controls'],['ports','Probe input'],['rear','Rear']].map(([v,l])=><button data-view={v}>{l}</button>)}</div><small id="model-state" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</small><p>Drag to orbit; pinch or scroll to zoom. Click the CH1 plug to disconnect, the empty CH1 socket to reconnect, or the single key to acquire. Click the vertical scale, timebase or trigger-level knob to increment (Shift-click to decrement). External sources route the free probe end away from the compensator; the external circuit is not drawn. The yellow trace on the instrument is the same capture shown below.</p>
<button id="plug" aria-pressed="true">Disconnect CH1</button></section>
<section class="s-panel"><p class="eq-meta">02 / ACQUISITION</p><h3>CH1 setup</h3><form id="scope-form" onsubmit="return false">
<label>Signal source<select id="signal"><option value="comp">Probe-compensator square</option><option value="rc">RC pulse response</option><option value="sine">1 kHz reference sine</option><option value="import">Imported trace</option></select></label>
<label>Sine peak (V)<input id="amplitude" type="number" min=".000001" max="10" step="any" value="1"/></label>
<label>Acquisition clock (S/s)<input id="rate" type="number" min="10" max="2000000" step="any" value="1000000"/></label>
<label>Time/div (ms)<input id="time" type="number" min=".01" max="10000" step="any" value=".5"/></label>
<label>Vertical scale (V/div)<input id="scale" type="number" min=".000001" max="10" step="any" value=".5"/></label>
<label>Vertical center (V)<input id="center" type="number" min="-100" max="100" step="any" value="1.25"/></label>
<label>Trigger level (V)<input id="level" type="number" min="-100" max="100" step="any" value="1"/></label>
<label>Trigger edge<select id="edge"><option>rising</option><option>falling</option></select></label>
<label>Input coupling<select id="coupling"><option>DC</option><option>AC</option></select></label>
<label>Probe readout factor<select id="factor"><option value="10">10× (matched)</option><option value="1">1× (mismatch demo)</option></select></label></form>
<div class="tools"><button class="run" id="acquire">Single acquisition</button><button id="restore">Restore example</button></div><p id="scope-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
<details><summary>Import a simulation trace</summary><p>Load a uniformly sampled voltage CSV, a Cortex Lab signal CSV (first voltage column, including µV), or a <code>bts.analog-waveform.v1</code> JSON. Imports stay on your computer. The first two samples must be time-ordered; the full clock is checked. Import chooses an initial view; then set a useful trigger level.</p><input type="file" id="input-file" accept=".csv,.json,text/csv,application/json"/><p><a href="/cortex/">Open Cortex Lab</a> and export a signal CSV, or try the <a href={asset+'example-lockin-capture.csv'} download>reference sine capture</a>.</p></details>
</section></div>
<section class="s-panel"><p class="eq-meta">03 / READOUT</p><h3>Triggered voltage</h3><canvas id="scope-trace" width="1100" height="370" aria-label="Sampled voltage versus trigger-relative time"></canvas><p id="measurement" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="scope-cursors"><label>Cursor A · sample index<input type="range" id="cursor-a" min="0" max="5000" value="0"/></label><label>Cursor B · sample index<input type="range" id="cursor-b" min="0" max="5000" value="0"/></label><output id="cursor-label"></output></div>
<div class="tools"><button id="save-csv">Download CSV</button><button id="save-json">Download capture JSON</button></div><p>CSV starts at the first returned sample. JSON retains trigger-relative seconds, the trigger index, the source clock origin, input metadata, volts and revision. Clipped traces are flagged, not silently rescaled.</p></section>
<section class="s-panel"><p class="eq-meta">04 / BENCH HANDOFF</p><h3>Read the same signal with a lock-in</h3><p>The <a href={asset+'example-lockin-capture.csv'} download>low-voltage scope capture</a> is a 1 kHz, 2 mV-peak sine acquired at 64 kS/s. Import it into the SR860 CSV input: the analytical RMS is 1.414214 mV; the lock-in recovered 1.414442 mV (±0.002 mV criterion). Do not substitute the 2.5 V calibrator: it overloads the lock-in’s 1 V peak input. <span id="downstream">The CSV retains the sample and contact IDs even without a connected station.</span></p><p><a href={asset+'interoperability.json'}>Cross-station test report and exact input checksums</a></p></section>
<section id="evidence" class="s-panel"><p class="eq-meta">05 / INSTRUMENT EVIDENCE</p><h3>Reference sheet</h3><p>Reconstructed MSO64B, 6-BW-1000, one CH1 TPP1000, handle upright, feet folded. These panels are original renders of the downloadable model, not photographs or factory CAD. Follow each link to the manufacturer’s illustrated evidence.</p><div class="scope-refs">{refs.map(([id,title,caption,url])=><figure><img src={asset+id+'.png'} alt={title+' original 3D view'} loading="lazy" width="600" height="400"/><figcaption><b>{title}</b><br/>{caption} <a href={url}>Compare source</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<div class="scope-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Value</th><th>Use and conditions</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{specs.map(([q,v,t,pg])=><tr><th>{q}</th><td>{v}</td><td>{t}</td><td><a href={ds+'#page='+pg}>Datasheet p. {pg}</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href="https://www.tek.com/en/datasheet/6series-b-mso-mixed-signal-oscilloscope-datasheet">Manufacturer datasheet</a> · <a href="https://www.tek.com/en/manual/oscilloscope/6-series-b-mso-6-series-b-mso-mixed-signal-oscilloscope-077169601">6 Series B service manual, front panel and display, fig. 8</a> · <a href="https://www.tek.com/en/datasheet/passive-voltage-probes">TPP1000 probe specifications</a>. No dimensioned accessory CAD or serial-specific rear photograph is asserted. The stock 1.3 m cable is shortened in the model to keep its connection visible.</p></section>
<section id="verification" class="s-panel"><p class="eq-meta">06 / NUMERICAL METHOD &amp; LIMITS</p><h3>From input voltage to cursor time</h3>
<p>The calibration source is an ideal periodic pulse. Its loaded level is 2.5 × 10 MΩ / (10 MΩ + 1 kΩ). The RC example solves a 1 kΩ / 100 nF circuit driven by a 0–1 V square in exact periodic steady state, with V(t) = V∞ + (V₀ − V∞) exp(−t/RC). The sine fixture uses sin(2πft). Built-in values are simulated, not measured. External traces are already voltages at the probe tip, interpolated linearly on the acquisition clock; they are not reloaded electrically.</p>
<p>Voltage is divided by the ideal 10× probe then multiplied by the selected indicated factor. AC coupling uses an illustrative 10 Hz first-order discrete high-pass, α = τ/(τ + Δt), with 100 ms preroll for generated sources; at the start of an import the filter assumes steady DC. Values are clipped and rounded to 4096 codes across ten vertical divisions. The first sampled threshold crossing after the pretrigger window defines t=0; there is no interpolated or sub-sample hardware timing claim. Cursor separation is Δindex / sample rate. Records include both endpoints of ten horizontal divisions. RMS is the unweighted discrete RMS over the returned samples.</p>
<p><b>Supported:</b> CH1, one edge trigger, effective acquisition clock 10 S/s–2 MS/s (linear interpolation when the imported source clock is slower); not a claim of native low-rate hardware modes, 16–65,536 samples per screen. We do not model GHz bandwidth, real probe capacitance, thermal noise, hardware timebase jitter, High Res decimation, or anti-alias filtering. Undersampling can alias. Unreachable trigger, disconnected input, out-of-range settings and truncated imports stop the run. No hardware trace was used to calibrate this solver.</p>
<h4>Reference checks</h4><div class="scope-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Computed</th><th>Criterion</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody id="test-rows"></tbody></table></div>
<div class="tools"><a href={asset+'acceptance.md'}>Preregistered cases</a><a href={asset+'verification.json'}>Verification report</a><a href={asset+'build-model.py'} download>Editable model source</a><a href={asset+'mso64b.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={asset+'solver.mjs'}>Acquisition solver</a><a href={asset+'schema.json'}>Capture schema</a><a href={asset+'example-capture.csv'} download>Example CSV</a></div><p><b>VR integration:</b> The <a href={asset+'vr-adapter.mjs'}>renderer-independent adapter</a> maps stable mesh names to connect, acquire and dial actions. The <a href={asset+'vr-manifest.json'}>VR manifest</a> gives bounds, units, ray targets, controller semantics and draw/mesh budget. The model is suitable for importing into a VR scene; this page itself provides non-immersive desktop and mobile interaction, not a verified Quest session.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/09-04/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>
#scope09{font-size:1.03rem}#scope09 h3{font-size:1.5rem;margin:.25rem 0 .8rem}#scope09 h4{font-size:1.15rem}#scope09 .scope-grid,#scope09 .scope-refs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#scope09 .s-panel{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#scope09 .scope-grid .s-panel{margin:0}#scope09 .eq-meta{margin:0;color:var(--text-muted,inherit)}#scope09 .scope-view{height:clamp(270px,32vw,430px);background:#1f2a32}#scope-3d{width:100%;height:100%;touch-action:none;display:block}#scope09 .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin:.6rem 0}#scope09 button,#scope09 input,#scope09 select{background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:2px;font:inherit;padding:.42rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#scope09 button{cursor:pointer}#scope09 button:disabled{opacity:.5}#scope09 .run{background:#335d57;color:white}#scope-form,#scope09 .scope-cursors{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.55rem}#scope09 label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.15rem;min-width:0}#scope09 label input,#scope09 label select{width:100%}#scope09 #scope-trace{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:#101b22}#scope09 .scope-cursors output{grid-column:1/-1}#scope09 .scope-refs img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:#253039}#scope09 figure{margin:.4rem 0}#scope09 figcaption{font-size:.9rem;margin:.5rem 0}#scope09 table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.9rem}#scope09 th,#scope09 td{text-align:left;padding:.5rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#scope09 .scope-scroll{overflow:auto}#scope-status[data-error="yes"]{border-left:4px solid #ad5037;padding-left:.5rem}#scope09 details{margin-top:1rem}#scope09 button:focus-visible,#scope09 select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #4ea1bf}
@media(max-width:780px){#scope09 .scope-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}#scope09 .scope-view{height:330px}}@media(max-width:520px){#scope09 .scope-refs{grid-template-columns:1fr}#scope09 .s-panel{padding:.7rem}#scope09 button{min-height:42px}#scope09 .scope-view{height:270px}}
</style>
